{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1087594-feeding-and-interacting-with-ghosts","id":1087594,"title":"feeding and interacting with ghosts","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-05-04T03:02:19-07:00","id":1087594,"title":"feeding and interacting with ghosts","content":"is there any disciplines (first or second ed) that allows a vampire to feed from a ghost?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4045-princeofcincinnati","name":"princeofcincinnati","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4045_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-04T03:30:14-07:00","id":1087601,"title":"","content":"There's Essentiaphagia from the Ordo Dracul book. It's a Bloodline Discipline, but in my group we've used it as a rarer Discipline that isn't exclusive to a Bloodline.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-04T04:21:13-07:00","id":1087618,"title":"","content":"1st edition has the disciplines Essentiaphagia, Carrefour, Thanatology, and Blood Tenebrous. It also has the Taste of the Strange merit. 2nd edition has the Unnatural Affinity merit and the 2nd edition version of Protean could theoretically work.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-04T04:24:56-07:00","id":1087620,"title":"","content":"Essentiaphagia, and there's a Ghost Eater Merit in Book of the Dead. It requires an impressive safari down into the Underworld to learn, but once you've learned to drink from the ghosts you can touch in the Underworld, you can carry that knowledge out to parasitize ghosts in Twilight by touching their anchors.<br /> <br /> Blood Tenebrous won't help with ghosts, and isn't especially convenient for feeding from spirits either, as you have to make the journey into the Shadow Realm to touch them. Carrefour will let you interact with ghosts, but not feed from them. Unnatural Affinity explicitly doesn't provide the ability to feed from beings you couldn't feed from otherwise \u2013 it just makes the result nourish like Kindred blood. Primeval Miasma wouldn't do the trick either in any situation where regular fangs wouldn't cut it.<br /> <br /> Thanatology works, but the ghost needs to be material, and Thanatology can't make it materialize.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":522,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","user":"Stupid Loserman","date":". 05-04-2017, 07:36 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-04T07:41:05-07:00","id":1087679,"title":"","content":"Blood Tenebrous converts numia to vitae. If the ghost has numia it can be fed from.<br /> <br /> Carrefour can be used to trap a ghost. You refuse to release it unless it uses its numia to provide you with sustenance. Just make sure you trap a ghost with that capability.<br /> <br /> Unnatural Affinity DOES let you feed from ghosts. It doesn't give you the ability to force them to materialize or travel to a zone where you can physically interact with them.<br /> <br /> You don't need Primeval Miasma. You grow yourself a head of Cerberus with the power at level 2 and select the special ability it grants you as &quot;ghost consumption&quot; while you have that head active.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5466,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","user":"tsusasi","date":". 05-04-2017, 10:43 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-04T08:22:11-07:00","id":1087708,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tsusasi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1087594-feeding-and-interacting-with-ghosts?p=1087679#post1087679\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Blood Tenebrous converts numia to vitae. If the ghost has numia it can be fed from.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's not at all how it works. Also, the only dot that doesn't explicitly work only on spirits or spiritual phenomena is the dot that lets you convert Vitae to Essence, and even then it's up for the ST to decide whether that Essence can be used by ghosts.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tsusasi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1087594-feeding-and-interacting-with-ghosts?p=1087679#post1087679\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Carrefour can be used to trap a ghost. You refuse to release it unless it uses its numia to provide you with sustenance. Just make sure you trap a ghost with that capability.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think any of the published Numina can convert Essence to Vitae. It'd require talking it through with the ST and the ST letting you &quot;find&quot; a ghost with such a highly specific Numen.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tsusasi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1087594-feeding-and-interacting-with-ghosts?p=1087679#post1087679\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You don't need Primeval Miasma. You grow yourself a head of Cerberus with the power at level 2 and select the special ability it grants you as &quot;ghost consumption&quot; while you have that head active.</div> </div> </div> </div>The second dot only grants abilities that mundane animals have. The fourth dot can grant you powers that are supernatural (the claws that aren't downgraded to bashing by victim vampires), but even then it's far from certain that Protean 4 would be able to create that kind of ability. The focus is still traits that mundane animals have; just improved.<br /> <br /> <br /> But I do agree with your take on Unnatural Affinity. Ghosts are even an example of creatures that can be chosen when buying that Merit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-04T12:23:56-07:00","id":1087853,"title":"","content":"It would seem that there is disagreements. What book is Unnatural Affinity in?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4045-princeofcincinnati","name":"princeofcincinnati","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4045_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-04T12:27:53-07:00","id":1087856,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>princeofcincinnati</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1087594-feeding-and-interacting-with-ghosts?p=1087853#post1087853\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It would seem that there is disagreements. What book is Unnatural Affinity in?</div> </div> </div> </div>Vampire: the Requiem Second Edition.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-04T12:32:41-07:00","id":1087859,"title":"","content":"Second edition core, p114.<br /> <br /> It's an alternative to drinking vampire blood at certain Blood Potencies, as each counts as Kindred blood and it allows you to obtain Vitae from any supernaturals, though the hard work is still up to you. You can eat from a spirit, but you don't gain any special ability to go to the spirit world. You can eat from a ghost but it doesn't give you any special ability to sense and attack ghosts.<br /> <br /> Each dot lets you pick a different being. So just one dot would let you get ghosts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-08T01:57:26-07:00","id":1089650,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1087594-feeding-and-interacting-with-ghosts?p=1087859#post1087859\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Second edition core, p114.<br /> <br /> It's an alternative to drinking vampire blood at certain Blood Potencies, as each counts as Kindred blood and it allows you to obtain Vitae from any supernaturals, though the hard work is still up to you. You can eat from a spirit, but you don't gain any special ability to go to the spirit world. You can eat from a ghost but it doesn't give you any special ability to sense and attack ghosts.<br /> <br /> Each dot lets you pick a different being. So just one dot would let you get ghosts.</div> </div> </div> </div>To add to this, the easiest way to then feed on ghosts is to find an averian gate and learn it's key to enter the underworld. There is no twilight in the underworld so all ghosts are manifested and easier to feed off of.<br /> <br /> An alternative would be possibly to look into the &quot;mortal interaction&quot; rules and likely get a ghoul or thrall to help a ghost manifest.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x","name":"Mr.F.I.X.","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2909_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1053"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}